# Forbidden-pattern list for the pre-commit / commit-msg privacy hooks and for
# scripts/check-secrets.sh.
#
# Copy this to  patterns.local  (gitignored) and fill in YOUR machine's real
# values, so they are enforced locally and can never be committed to this public
# repo. One POSIX extended-regex per line; blank lines and "#" comments ignored;
# matching is case-insensitive.
#
# Use SPECIFIC values, not broad regexes, so legitimate placeholders in the repo
# (documentation IPs, <PLACEHOLDER> tokens in DROPLET.md) don't trip the hook.
#
# NOTE: patterns for *shapes* (private IP ranges, private-key headers, token
# formats) do NOT belong here — they describe a form rather than a value, so they
# are safe to publish and live directly in scripts/check-secrets.sh.
#
# Examples:
#
#   my-hostname                # the droplet's hostname
#   203\.0\.113\.[0-9]+        # its public IP (RFC5737 example shown)
#   /home/myuser               # real server home path
#   mysurname                  # anything that deanonymizes you
#   me@example\.com            # personal email
#   \b12345\b                  # a real ZIP that leaked via a joke address
#
# Activate the hooks once:  git config core.hooksPath .githooks
